
.TH "WSLVIEW" "1" "DATEPLACEHOLDER" "VERSIONPLACEHOLDER" "WSL Utilities User Manual"
.SH NAME
.B wslview, wview, wslstart, wstart
- Component of WSL Utilities
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wslview
.RB [ OPTIONS ]
.I LINK_OR_FILE
.RI [ LINK_OR_FILE ...]
.PP
.B wslview \-\-reveal \fIPATH\fR
.PP
.B wslview
.BR \-r | \-u | \-e
.PP
.B wslview
.RB [ \-hv ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
This is a file viewer on WSL that allows you to open files and folders from WSL in Windows and a fake web browser that allows opening urls in your default browser on Windows 10. Multiple \fILINK_OR_FILE\fR arguments are accepted; every argument is opened separately.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -h, --help
print a simple help.
.TP
.B -v, --version
print current version.
.TP
.B -E, --engine \fIENGINE\fR
Select \fBpowershell\fR, \fBcmd\fR, or \fBcmd_explorer\fR as the Windows launcher.
.TP
.B -s, --skip-validation-check
Skip the curl HTTP HEAD probe. A failed probe normally leaves the original URL unchanged and does not convert it to a filesystem path.
.TP
.B --reveal \fIPATH\fR
Highlight \fIPATH\fR in its Windows Explorer folder instead of opening it. \fIPATH\fR must be an existing Linux path or a Windows path; this option cannot be combined with \fILINK_OR_FILE\fR.
.TP
.B -u, --unreg-as-browser
Remove wslview browser registration. This action accepts no LINK_OR_FILE or launch options.
.TP
.B -r, --reg-as-browser
Register wslview through update-alternatives. This action accepts no LINK_OR_FILE or launch options.
.TP
.B -e, --export-as-browser
Set BROWSER in existing .bashrc, .zshrc, and .kshrc files. This action accepts no LINK_OR_FILE or launch options.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.TP
.B WSLVIEW_DEFAULT_ENGINE
default method to start websites/folders/files. Default type is "powershell". Here are all available options:
.nf
.in +4
powershell: use the Windows Shell application association through powershell.exe
cmd: compatibility alias for the PowerShell shell launcher
cmd_explorer: use explorer.exe directly
.in
.fi
.TP
.B WSLVIEW_SKIP_VALIDATION_CHECK
whether to skip validation check. Default is 1, which is not skipping. Can be either `0` or `1`.
.SH NOTES
Opening a file stored in the Linux filesystem launches it through the
.B \e\ewsl.localhost\e\eDISTRO\e\e
network share. Windows treats this share as a location outside the local network, so opening such a file may show an
"Open File - Security Warning" dialog. To stop the prompt, add the share host to the Local intranet zone once per Windows user:
.PP
.RS
.nf
reg.exe add "HKCU\\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\ZoneMap\\Domains\\wsl.localhost" /v file /t REG_DWORD /d 1 /f
.fi
.RE
.PP
Use
.B wsl$
instead of
.B wsl.localhost
for setups still relying on the legacy share name. Revert by deleting the added registry value.
